  {title:'Each, one of and compound subjects',terms:[['compound subject','two subjects joined together']],explain:'“Each” and “one” normally control singular verbs; subjects joined by “and” normally take plural verbs.',example:'“Each pupil has a pencil.” “Mother and father are home.”',check:'Why is “Each pupil have” incorrect in standard English?'}
